igital-inc-v-pivium-inc/", "date_created": "2025-04-11T17:05:35.259818-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-04-11T17:05:35.273152-07:00", "sha1": "", "page_count": null, "file_size": null, "filepath_local": null, "filepath_ia": "", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "", "ocr_status": null, "date_upload": null, "document_number": "19", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035025622644", "is_available": false, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "Answer to Amended Complaint AND Counterclaim", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2025-04-11T17:05:35.175307-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-04-11T17:05:35.188313-07:00", "date_filed": "2025-04-11", "time_filed": "16:57:41", "entry_number": 19, "recap_sequence_number": "2025-04-11.001", "pacer_sequence_number": 52, "description": "", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/418203229/", "id": 418203229, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/69476214/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/431994697/", "id": 431994697, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "/docket/69476214/18/join-digital-inc-v-pivium-inc/", "date_created": "2025-03-04T10:05:33.119318-08:00", "date_modified": "2025-04-04T01:56:25.769420-07:00", "sha1": "eec3d8d085f5ddf7df3697deed86a818cdc4ea4c", "page_count": 3, "file_size": 204428, "filepath_local": "recap/gov.uscourts.cand.441339/gov.uscourts.cand.441339.18.0.pdf", "filepath_ia": "https://archive.org/download/gov.uscourts.cand.441339/gov.uscourts.cand.441339.18.0.pdf", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "         Case 3:24-cv-09138-HSG            Document 18         Filed 03/04/25   Page 1 of 3\n\n\n 1   Stephen D. Finestone (Cal. Bar. No. 125675)\n     Michael J. Coffino (Cal. Bar No. 88109)\n 2   FINESTONE HAYES LLP\n     456 Montgomery Street, Suite 1300\n 3\n     San Francisco, CA 94104\n 4   Tel.: (415) 481-5481\n     Fax: (415) 398-2820\n 5   Email: sfinestone@fhlawllp.com\n     Email: mcoffino@fhlawllp.com\n 6\n     Attorneys for Plaintiff Join Digital, Inc.\n 7\n\n 8                            UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n                            NORTHERN DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\n 9                               SAN FRANCISCO DIVISION\n10\n      Join Digital, Inc.,                                  Case No. 24-cv-09138-HSG\n11\n              Plaintiff,\n12\n                                                           REVISED STIPULATION TO\n13           v.                                            CONTINUE CASE MANAGEMENT\n                                                           CONFERENCE AND RELATED\n14    Pivium, Inc.,                                        DEADLINES AND ORDER (as\n                                                           modified)\n15            Defendant.\n16\n\n17      Plaintiff Join Digital, Inc. (\u201cJoin Digital\u201d) and Defendant Pivium, Inc. (\u201cPivium\u201d) have\n18   selected a mediator and scheduled a mediation and toward that end seek to continue certain dates\n19   the Court has set regarding the case management conference. Accordingly, pursuant to Civil\n20   L.Rs. 7-12 and 16(2)(e), the parties have stipulated as follows subject to Court approval.\n21                                                STIPULATION\n22      This stipulation is made with reference to the following:\n23      1. Join Digital filed a Complaint against Pivium on December 17, 2024 (ECF 1).\n24      2. On December 18, 2024, the Court issued an Order Setting Initial Case Management\n25   Conference and ADR Deadlines (\u201cInitial CMC Order\u201d) (ECF 3) with the following dates:\n26          a. February 28, 2025: Deadline to file ADR Certification\n27\n                                                       1\n28\n         STIPULATION AND ORDER TO CONTINUE CASE MANAGEMENT CONFERENCE AND\n                                  RELATED DEADLINES\n\f         Case 3:24-cv-09138-HSG           Document 18       Filed 03/04/25      Page 2 of 3\n\n\n 1          b. February 28, 2025: Deadline to meet and confer re: initial disclosures, early\n\n 2              settlement, ADR process selection, and discovery plan.\n\n 3          c. March 14, 2025: Deadline to make initial disclosures\n\n 4          d. March 14, 2025: Deadline to file Joint Case Management Statement\n\n 5          e. March 21, 2025 at 2:00 p.m.: Initial Case Management Conference.\n\n 6      3. Soon thereafter, the parties, through counsel, had preliminary discussions about scheduling\n\n 7   a mediation.\n\n 8      4. Join Digital served the Complaint on Pivium on January 29, 2025.\n\n 9      5. Join Digital filed a First Amended Complaint (\u201cFAC\u201d) on February 11, 2025 (ECF 5).\n\n10      6. That same day, the parties entered into a stipulation pursuant to which counsel for Pivium\n\n11   accepted service of the FAC on behalf of Pivium and Join Digital agreed that Pivium may have\n\n12   until April 14, 2025 to respond to the FAC (ECF 6, misfiled as a First Amended Complaint).\n\n13      7. One of the parties declined to consent to Magistrate Judge jurisdiction (ECF 12 and 14)\n\n14   and the Court reassigned this action to the Hon. Haywood S. Gilliam, Jr.\n\n15      8. Following the reassignment, on February 27, 2025, the Court scheduled a case\n\n16   management conference for March 25, 2025 at 2 p.m. (ECF 15).\n\n17      9. The parties have selected a mediator and scheduled April 28, 2025 as a tentative date for\n\n18   the mediation.\n\n19      10. The parties wish at this time to focus on seeking a consensual resolution without\n\n20   incurring significant expense and for that reason wish to reschedule the Case Management\n\n21   Conference and reset all related dates.\n\n22          Accordingly, the parties seek an order that provides the following dates:\n\n23      a. April 30, 2025: Deadline to file ADR Certification\n\n24      b. April 30, 2025: Deadline to meet and confer re: initial disclosures, early settlement, ADR\n\n25          process selection, and discovery plan.\n\n26      c. May 21, 2025: Deadline to make initial disclosures\n\n27\n                                                     2\n28\n         STIPULATION AND ORDER TO CONTINUE CASE MANAGEMENT CONFERENCE AND\n                                  RELATED DEADLINES\n\f         Case 3:24-cv-09138-HSG           Document 18        Filed 03/04/25        Page 3 of 3\n\n\n 1      d. May 21, 2025: Deadline to file Joint Case Management Statement\n\n 2      e. June 3, 2025 at 2:00 p.m.: Initial Case Management Conference\n\n 3          If the court is not available on June 3, 2025 for the Initial Case Management Conference,\n\n 4   the parties are available for a case management conference at a later date.\n\n 5      IT IS SO STIPULATED\n\n 6   Dated: March 3, 2025\n\n 7   Finestone Hayes LLP\n\n 8     /s/ Michael J. Coffino\n     By: Michael J. Coffino (SBN 88109)\n 9   Attorneys for Join Digital, Inc.\n10   Nixon Peabody LLP\n11     /s/ Corey T. Legget\n     By: Corey Leggett (SBN 342972)\n12\n     Jason C. Kravitz\n13   Counsel for Pivium, Inc.\n\n14                                                ORDER\n15          Based on the stipulation of the parties and good cause appearing,\n16          IT IS SO ORDERED . The Zoom webinar information and\n17          instructions remain the same as previously provided in docket\n18          nos. 15 and 16.\n19   DATED: 3/4/2025                                        ______________________________\n20                                                              Hon. Haywood S. Gilliam, Jr.\n                                                                District Court Judge\n21\n\n22\n\n23\n\n24\n\n25\n\n26\n\n27\n                                                      3\n28\n         STIPULATION AND ORDER TO CONTINUE CASE MANAGEMENT CONFERENCE AND\n                                  RELATED DEADLINES\n\f", "ocr_status": 2, "date_upload": "2025-03-05T03:18:05.800012-08:00", "document_number": "18", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035025471525", "is_available": true, "is_free_on_pacer": true, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "Order AND ~Util - Set Deadlines/Hearings AND ~Util - Terminate Motions", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2025-03-04T10:05:33.107356-08:00", "date_modified": "2025-04-04T01:56:25.758496-07:00", "date_filed": "2025-03-04", "time_filed": "09:50:33", "entry_number": 18, "recap_sequence_number": "2025-03-04.001", "pacer_sequence_number": 47, "description": " ORDER (as modified) GRANTING Revised Stipulation and Order Regarding CMC and Related Deadlines.  Signed by Judge Haywood S. Gilliam, Jr. on 3/4/2025.  Case Management Statement due by 5/21/2025.  Initial Case Management Conference set for 6/3/2025 02:00 PM via a Zoom webinar.The Zoom webinar information and instructions remain the same as previously provided in docket nos.  15  and  16 . (ndr, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/4/2025)", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/418071574/", "id": 418071574, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/69476214/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/431859426/", "id": 431859426, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "/docket/69476214/17/join-digital-inc-v-pivium-inc/", "date_created": "2025-03-03T09:32:31.168640-08:00", "date_modified": "2025-03-03T10:07:43.572967-08:00", "sha1": "", "page_count": null, "file_size": null, "filepath_local": null, "filepath_ia": "", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "", "ocr_status": null, "date_upload": null, "document_number": "17", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035025465754", "is_available": false, "is_free_on_pacer": nu